|     When the text is longer than ``limit`` it is cut and ``suffix`` is appended\n   12|     to show that content was removed.\n   13| \n   14|     Args:\n   15|         text: Input text.\n   16|         limit: Maximum length of the returned string, including ``suffix``.\n   17|         suffix: Marker appended when the text was shortened.\n   18| \n   19|     Returns:\n   20|         The original text when it already fits, otherwise a shortened version.\n   21| \n   22|     Raises:\n   23|         ValueError: If ``limit`` is negative.\n   24|     \"\"\"\n   25|     if limit < 0:\n   26|         raise ValueError(\"limit must not be negative\")\n   27|     if len(text) <= limit:\n   28|         return text\n   29|     return text[:limit] + suffix"},"truncated":false},{"seq":15,"ts":"2026-11-20T19:19:59.110133","event_type":"tool.call","payload":{"tool":"read_file","arguments":{"path":"tests/test_truncate.py"},"step":2},"truncated":false},{"seq":16,"ts":"2026-11-20T19:19:59.190263","event_type":"file.read","payload":{"path":"tests/test_truncate.py","chars":582,"tool":"read_file"},"truncated":false},{"seq":17,"ts":"2026-11-20T19:19:59.191479","event_type":"tool.result","payload":{"tool":"read_file","ok":true,"result_chars":770,"result_preview":"    1| \"\"\"Pre-existing truncate tests.\n    2| \n    3| ``test_short_text_is_returned_unchanged`` is the regression trap for the\n    4| truncate task: the obvious \"just always cut and append the suffix\" fix breaks\n    5| it.\n    6| \"\"\"\n    7| \n    8| import pytest\n    9| \n   10| from textkit import truncate\n   11| \n   12| \n   13| def test_short_text_is_returned_unchanged():\n   14|     assert truncate(\"hello\", 10) == \"hello\"\n   15| \n   16| \n   17| def test_exact_length_is_returned_unchanged():\n   18|     assert truncate(\"hello\", 5) == \"hello\"\n   19| \n   20| \n   21| def test_empty_text():\n   22|     assert truncate(\"\", 5) == \"\"\n   23| \n   24| \n   25| def test_negative_limit_rejected():\n  